Soman Chainani: Have you heard of this guy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:25.840 --> 00:34:29.144
named Christopher Marley?
Tim Ferriss: No.&nbsp;

00:34:29.144 --> 00:34:37.520
Soman Chainani: He is an artist, but his&nbsp;
canvas only works with preserved animals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:37.520 --> 00:34:40.920
from strange parts of the Earth.
Tim Ferriss: Tell me more.&nbsp;

00:34:40.920 --> 00:34:46.600
Soman Chainani: He's almost like Indiana Jones.&nbsp;
He works with remote tribes in the Amazon. He'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:46.600 --> 00:34:53.707
just go all over the Earth to find animals we've&nbsp;
never seen before, and then makes art out of them.&nbsp;

00:34:53.707 --> 00:34:56.880
Tim Ferriss: Christopher Marley?
Soman Chainani: Christopher Marley. And so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:56.880 --> 00:35:02.240
I have all of his books, and I saw an exhibition&nbsp;
of his in person, and it was the most inspiring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:02.240 --> 00:35:05.984
beautiful thing I have ever seen.
Tim Ferriss: That's a strong statement.&nbsp;

00:35:05.984 --> 00:35:07.520
Soman Chainani: It is.
Tim Ferriss: And that's coming from someone who's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:07.520 --> 00:35:11.200
exposed to art. You're exposed to all that art.
Soman Chainani: Art is my life, yeah, but this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:11.200 --> 00:35:15.680
is because they're real animals. And so the idea&nbsp;
of, I spend my life creating fantasies. And then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:15.680 --> 00:35:21.880
to see that the real world has more fantastical&nbsp;
things than you'll ever see. And he has so many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:21.880 --> 00:35:25.920
great ones where you'll see, he'll just make art&nbsp;
out of maybe a thousand butterflies that he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:25.920 --> 00:35:29.640
collected. But the colors of the butterflies,&nbsp;
you've never seen stuff like this before.&nbsp;

00:35:29.640 --> 00:35:34.240
It's almost like when you think of the deep sea&nbsp;
fish that you've never seen before. He's finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:34.240 --> 00:35:39.960
this up on land. So the beetles, the snakes,&nbsp;
the this. But then he has this additional talent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:39.960 --> 00:35:47.360
of making the most spectacular art out of it&nbsp;
so that it almost looks — if they were fake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:47.360 --> 00:35:52.400
it would still be equally impressive. So the fact&nbsp;
that he's going there, making these relationships,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:52.400 --> 00:35:59.560
getting animals that — convincing these tribes&nbsp;
to hold onto animals that they find for him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:59.560 --> 00:36:02.840
The whole thing's insane. And the fact that this&nbsp;
guy isn't the most famous person in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:02.840 --> 00:36:04.640
to me, is shocking.
Tim Ferriss: How did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:04.640 --> 00:36:09.160
