Soman Chainani: I was in North Carolina&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:09.160 --> 00:36:13.760
taking — we were on a family reunion trip and&nbsp;
we went to the museum with my niece and nephew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:13.760 --> 00:36:20.400
who were teenagers. And that was the little fun&nbsp;
thing. And then I bought all his books, I followed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:20.400 --> 00:36:24.184
him on Instagram, and I just think it's the most —
Tim Ferriss: Amazing. All right.&nbsp;

00:36:24.184 --> 00:36:28.120
Soman Chainani: Yeah. As soon as you start looking&nbsp;
at his art, you're going to be like — and also he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:28.120 --> 00:36:34.200
has a crazy story, which is, they had a photo&nbsp;
of him up on the wall. And I was like, "That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:34.200 --> 00:36:43.280
him?" He was a supermodel. He was a supermodel,&nbsp;
this rugged supermodel who then, I don't know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:43.280 --> 00:36:48.720
used his wealth to then do what he really&nbsp;
wanted to do, which was like be Indiana Jones.&nbsp;

00:36:48.720 --> 00:36:52.160
Tim Ferriss: That's incredible.
Soman Chainani: But the talent is insane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:52.160 --> 00:36:56.680
the way he places everything. I almost want&nbsp;
to pause for a second and show you the art.&nbsp;

00:36:56.680 --> 00:36:59.240
Tim Ferriss: Let's do it.&nbsp;
Yeah, sure. Let me take a look.&nbsp;

00:36:59.240 --> 00:37:01.440
Soman Chainani: You have to see it&nbsp;
because once you see it you're going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:01.440 --> 00:37:08.187
to be like — hold on. You're going&nbsp;
to want to make him your best friend.&nbsp;

00:37:08.187 --> 00:37:12.904
Tim Ferriss: Oh, wow. Okay.&nbsp;
All right. That's wild.&nbsp;

00:37:12.904 --> 00:37:14.499
Soman Chainani: That's just one.
Tim Ferriss: That is wild.

00:37:14.499 --> 00:37:15.519
That's wild.
Soman Chainani: If you go back to the grade,

00:37:15.600 --> 00:37:20.680
you'll just see tons of them.
Tim Ferriss: Oh, yeah. Okay. So this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:20.680 --> 00:37:27.624
@christophermarleystudio, spelled like Bob Marley.&nbsp;
Christophermarleystudio. Almost 60,000 followers.&nbsp;

00:37:27.624 --> 00:37:32.200
Soman Chainani: It should be 60 million.
Tim Ferriss: "All vertebrates are reclaimed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:32.200 --> 00:37:35.633
specimens. None are killed for art." That was&nbsp;
going to be one of my questions. Okay, yes. All&nbsp;&nbsp;

