Soman Chainani: So I start watching it and I&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:31.560 --> 01:15:38.720
realize that this position of being a quarterback&nbsp;
is the greatest metaphor for what life should be&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:38.720 --> 01:15:42.400
because we all think we're the decision makers as&nbsp;
what we were talking about with follow the flow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:42.400 --> 01:15:46.680
We think we're the ones in charge of everything&nbsp;
like that. That's not what a quarterback is. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:46.680 --> 01:15:52.800
quarterback knows all the possible plays. The&nbsp;
other forces are calling it into his helmet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:52.800 --> 01:15:57.560
He's not even able to talk to the coach. He can't&nbsp;
talk back to the coach. It's a one-way system. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:57.560 --> 01:16:03.720
literally, it's the universe telling him what the&nbsp;
play is. So he's hearing, "White squall, Madonna,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:03.720 --> 01:16:09.960
six, wing," whatever. He's like, "Okay. Execute."&nbsp;
Right? So that's it. And I feel like that's what&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:09.960 --> 01:16:14.960
life should be. You're in the flow so much that&nbsp;
the orders are coming from outside. Orders are&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:14.960 --> 01:16:18.480
coming from outside telling you what the play is.
You get the play. You go into the huddle. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:18.480 --> 01:16:22.760
communicate the play to your whole team. Now,&nbsp;
everybody's on the same page as you. You've&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:22.760 --> 01:16:27.720
got everyone with you now. You go into&nbsp;
the huddle, the ball is snapped to you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:27.720 --> 01:16:34.880
and now you have to adjust, because the world's&nbsp;
going to react to your play. And that's where&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:34.880 --> 01:16:41.080
it gets interesting because you have to be so&nbsp;
present and in the moment that you can react to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:41.080 --> 01:16:45.160
what's going to happen. And to me, that's life.&nbsp;
Everyone's focused so much on deciding the play.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:45.160 --> 01:16:52.520
Don't focus on deciding the play. Once you feel&nbsp;
a play, execute it, just go, follow it. And if it&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:52.520 --> 01:16:57.800
busts, whatever. You've got a new play coming.
