01:17:45.640 --> 01:17:50.360
tenses up as they're about to hit the ball because&nbsp;
the pressure of hitting the right shot gets them&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:50.360 --> 01:17:58.360
at the last nanosecond. And his job is to stay&nbsp;
relaxed so he has an extra millisecond of options.&nbsp;

01:17:58.360 --> 01:18:04.360
And so, it was just something about that show&nbsp;
where I was like, "These guys are learning to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:04.360 --> 01:18:09.120
not be — they don't call the play, but&nbsp;
they're the executing guys." And I just&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:09.120 --> 01:18:15.160
think that's life. Let the plays come to you.&nbsp;
Let them come through your invisible headset.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:15.160 --> 01:18:20.440
Don't question it. You can't talk back to it.&nbsp;
Just take the play, and then execute. So there&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:20.440 --> 01:18:22.000
was something about that show. I don't know.
